# Trivy IaC ignore baseline — sandbox + accepted deviations
# Format: AVD-<provider>-<id>  # reason
#
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Terraform / AWS — sandbox architectural decisions
# These findings are intentional for the sandbox environment and documented in
# ADR-0027 (cloud-agnostic substrate) go-live conditions.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# S3 SSE-KMS with customer-managed key: sandbox uses SSE-S3 for cost optimisation.
# CMK rotation is a prod go-live condition (ADR-0027 C5).
AVD-AWS-0132

# EKS API server public endpoint: required for sandbox runner and developer access.
# Prod will use private endpoint + VPN (ADR-0027 go-live).
AVD-AWS-0040
AVD-AWS-0041

# IMDSv2 not enforced on runner EC2 instances: sandbox runner pool (aws/modules/runner)
# uses launch templates without http_tokens=required. Enforcing IMDSv2 is a prod
# go-live condition (ADR-0027 hardening). Scope: runner node pool only (not app nodes).
AVD-AWS-0028

# Root EBS volume unencrypted: runner EC2 instances (aws/modules/runner) use
# unencrypted root volumes. Encrypted volumes are a prod go-live condition (ADR-0027 C5).
AVD-AWS-0131

# Branch protection signed commits not required: GitHub branch protection in
# aws/envs/sandbox-platform/github-governance.tf. The main branch ruleset enforces
# GPG signature verification via the GitHub main-protection ruleset (not Terraform-managed);
# the Terraform resource manages secondary branches. Prod go-live condition.
AVD-GIT-0004

# Security group unrestricted egress: runner SGs need internet egress for
# CI builds (npm, gradle, docker pulls). Scope = runner pool only.
AVD-AWS-0104

# Subnet auto-assign public IP: required for NAT gateway, ALB, and runner nodes
# in the sandbox VPC public subnets.
AVD-AWS-0164

# CloudFront distribution without WAF: applies to the developer portal static
# distribution (static HTML/JS, no user-generated content). The ingress-nginx
# WAF (ModSecurity/OWASP CRS, ADR-0093) protects the API plane.
AVD-AWS-0011

# SNS topic KMS encryption: the CloudWatch NAT budget alarm (finops-budget.tf)
# uses a SNS notification topic without a customer-managed KMS key. The topic
# carries only operational alerts (no PII), and CMK encryption is a prod
# go-live condition (ADR-0027 C5). Sandbox cost-only scope.
AVD-AWS-0095

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Kubernetes — hardening follow-ups (tracked in issue #854 and related issues)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# readOnlyRootFilesystem: several containers (Keycloak theme cache, registry
# cache, GoAlert, Kafka-UI, nginx build-cache) need writable tmp/work dirs.
# Progressive hardening is tracked in the network-policy / security tier-2
# sweep (issue #854). Each container will be addressed individually.
AVD-KSV-0014

# ConfigMap storing secrets: Keycloak realm-mobile-settings ConfigMap contains
# a YAML key `# Offline token` (a comment explaining offline token config).
# Trivy DS/KSV-0109 false-positive: the key name starts with "#" — it is a YAML
# comment in the file, not a secret value.
AVD-KSV-0109

# Default security context (allows root privileges): applies to pyrra-api,
# pyrra-kubernetes, pact-broker, and registry-cache (ghcr-cache, quay-cache,
# registry-cache) third-party deployments. Security context tightening is a
# follow-up in the security tier-2 hardening sweep (#850-#854).
AVD-KSV-0118

# Service with externalName: the `grafana-tools` ExternalName Service in the
# `admin-ui` namespace (ADR-0234). KSV-0108 exists for CVE-2020-8554, where a
# Service pointing OUTSIDE the cluster lets a namespace-scoped actor intercept
# traffic to an arbitrary external IP. This one points at
# kube-prometheus-stack-grafana.observability.svc.cluster.local — an in-cluster
# name, resolved by CoreDNS, reachable only through an Ingress that gates every
# request against the admin-UI session. The check cannot tell the two apart.
#
# BLAST RADIUS, stated because a baseline entry is repo-wide: as of this commit
# that Service is the ONLY `type: ExternalName` in gitops. A second one would be
# silently exempted by this line, so `tools-gate.test.ts` asserts the count and
# fails the admin-ui suite if another appears — the exclusion stays a thing
# someone has to justify, not a default someone inherits.
AVD-KSV-0108
